      "title": "runDaemonStop is fail-open: probe failure or bootout failure falls back to a signal and reports success",
      "detail": "The stop gate gates on `st.Loaded` from `supervisorStateFor(sup.name)`; a probe failure returns `SupervisorState{Err: ..., Loaded: false}`, so the code silently skips the supervisor stop. Likewise, when `supervisorRun(sup.stop)` fails, `stoppedUnder` stays empty and control falls through to `stopDaemonDirect`, then prints 'Daemon stopped'. But the change's own comment (daemon.go:242-246) states a signal alone does not stop a supervised daemon: the loaded KeepAlive job respawns the process it manages. So both failure paths emit the same success value as the success path while leaving a loaded job that respawns the daemon. TestRunDaemonStop_SupervisorFailureFallsBackToASignal codifies this false success. Contrast the start path, which is fail-closed (`st.Err == nil \u0026\u0026 !st.Loaded` before bootstrap, and otherwise returns an error). Fix: on `st.Err != nil` or a failed bootout, either still attempt the supervisor stop (a supervisor file for this town is already confirmed) and/or return an error / print a prominent warning instead of reporting a stop that will not stay down."
