      "detail": "After `supervisorRun(sup.stop)` succeeds, launchd has already SIGTERMed the daemon; the `stillRunning` re-check can observe it mid-shutdown, and then `stopDaemonDirect` (`daemon.StopDaemon`) re-checks `IsRunning` internally and returns 'daemon is not running' if the process released the lock in between. `runDaemonStop` then reports an error even though the stop actually succeeded. This is a user-visible race in the common supervised-stop path (the old code had a narrower version of the same re-check gap)."
